My approach:
1. create an hash map and also an vector to store which elements are occured more than n/3 times
2. traverse the array and fill the hashmap and traverse through the hashmap and push which element occured more than n/3 times to the vector 
3. return the vector

Time complexity: O(2N) ~ O(N)
because we are running two for loops 
Space complexity: O(N)
because we are creating an hash map for each element in the array 

My code :
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> majorityElement(vector<int>& nums) {
        unordered_map<int,int> ump;
        vector<int> v;
        for(int i = 0;i<nums.size();i++){
            ump[nums[i]]++;
        }
        for(auto it: ump){
            if(it.second > (nums.size() / 3)) {
                v.push_back(it.first);
            }
        }
        return v;
    }
};
